1
00:00:01,084 --> 00:00:02,502
[ATTY. GRANADO] <i>Due to your withdrawal,</i>

2
00:00:02,585 --> 00:00:05,088
<i>the court dismissed Bea's cases</i>
<i>without prejudice.</i>

3
00:00:05,171 --> 00:00:07,173
<i>But we need to file for medical clearance.</i>

4
00:00:07,257 --> 00:00:08,675
<i>She can come home tomorrow.</i>

5
00:00:08,758 --> 00:00:10,719
<i>Okay, Attorney. Thank you.</i>

6
00:00:16,891 --> 00:00:19,019
- [BILLY GRUNTS SOFTLY]
<i>- Will you visit her, Billy?</i>

7
00:00:21,563 --> 00:00:24,357
<i>Dad's there. He can handle it.</i>

8
00:00:25,024 --> 00:00:28,028
<i>What about you? Can you handle it?</i>

9
00:00:28,111 --> 00:00:30,363
- [BILLY HALF-LAUGHS]
- [PRECIOUS] <i>Come on.</i>

10
00:00:31,239 --> 00:00:32,824
[PRECIOUS] <i>It's so good.</i>

11
00:00:32,907 --> 00:00:34,534
<i>Where's Oliver, Auntie?</i>

12
00:00:34,617 --> 00:00:36,161
<i>He's sleeping already.</i>

13
00:00:39,831 --> 00:00:41,374
<i>Is something wrong, Billy?</i>

14
00:00:44,878 --> 00:00:48,256
<i>I just don't know how to tell him that</i>

15
00:00:49,215 --> 00:00:51,009
<i>he has another sister.</i>

16
00:00:53,511 --> 00:00:56,514
<i>I wrote these letters</i>
<i>for you and your siblings.</i>

17
00:00:56,598 --> 00:01:00,685
<i>I expressed there</i>
<i>how much I missed all of you</i>

18
00:01:00,769 --> 00:01:02,353
<i>and how sorry I was.</i>

19
00:01:03,396 --> 00:01:06,858
[GENTLE MUSIC PLAYING]

20
00:01:18,620 --> 00:01:20,163
[SNIFFLES]

21
00:01:21,915 --> 00:01:24,459
<i>Even if I read these,</i>

22
00:01:25,752 --> 00:01:28,254
<i>nothing would change.</i>

23
00:01:30,048 --> 00:01:32,425
<i>It won't bring back…</i>

24
00:01:35,845 --> 00:01:37,305
<i>what I've lost.</i>

25
00:01:38,890 --> 00:01:43,228
<i>I don't expect you</i>
<i>to forgive me completely.</i>

26
00:01:46,022 --> 00:01:47,106
<i>But, my dear,</i>

27
00:01:48,274 --> 00:01:50,777
<i>please don't waste this opportunity…</i>

28
00:01:53,780 --> 00:01:55,698
<i>to start anew.</i>

29
00:01:56,950 --> 00:01:58,827
<i>I'm trying to start over too.</i>

30
00:02:01,204 --> 00:02:02,580
<i>With you</i>

31
00:02:04,207 --> 00:02:05,834
<i>and your siblings.</i>

32
00:02:12,423 --> 00:02:13,758
[BILLY] <i>You know, Oliver,</i>

33
00:02:13,842 --> 00:02:18,304
<i>sometimes, even grown-ups</i>

34
00:02:18,388 --> 00:02:20,765
<i>still keep secrets.</i>

35
00:02:28,106 --> 00:02:31,609
<i>Our dad's scared right now…</i>

36
00:02:33,570 --> 00:02:36,239
<i>because he kept a secret from us.</i>

37
00:02:38,366 --> 00:02:40,493
<i>What's his secret?</i>

38
00:02:43,413 --> 00:02:47,417
<i>I just found out recently…</i>

39
00:02:49,502 --> 00:02:52,130
<i>we have other siblings.</i>

40
00:02:52,213 --> 00:02:55,508
<i>If they're our siblings,</i>

41
00:02:55,592 --> 00:02:58,136
<i>why aren't they with us?</i>

42
00:02:58,219 --> 00:03:01,681
<i>What matters is you know the truth now.</i>

43
00:03:05,685 --> 00:03:07,729
<i>Where are they?</i>

44
00:03:07,812 --> 00:03:10,106
<i>Where are we going to meet them?</i>

45
00:03:10,189 --> 00:03:13,651
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

46
00:03:30,209 --> 00:03:36,466
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

47
00:04:37,151 --> 00:04:38,861
She's doing well now.

48
00:04:38,945 --> 00:04:43,533
All her vitals are stable,
no complications.

49
00:04:44,117 --> 00:04:45,743
She's ready to be discharged.

50
00:04:46,953 --> 00:04:48,705
- Thank you, Doc.
- [DOOR OPENS]

51
00:05:01,259 --> 00:05:03,011
- [BREATHES SOFTLY]
- Come on.

52
00:05:07,974 --> 00:05:13,187
[MELLOW MUSIC PLAYING]

53
00:05:13,271 --> 00:05:15,648
[BEA] Oliver? Oliver, right?

54
00:05:15,732 --> 00:05:21,988
[MELLOW MUSIC CONTINUES]

55
00:05:26,117 --> 00:05:29,078
Uh… I'm Bea.

56
00:05:32,498 --> 00:05:33,958
I'm your sister too.

57
00:05:36,002 --> 00:05:37,462
If you want,

58
00:05:37,545 --> 00:05:40,465
you can call me

59
00:05:40,548 --> 00:05:41,758
Big Sister Bea.

60
00:05:42,550 --> 00:05:47,430
I've heard so many
wonderful stories about you.

61
00:05:47,513 --> 00:05:50,224
Papa says you're super smart.

62
00:05:50,808 --> 00:05:55,271
I guess you take after Billy.

63
00:05:56,606 --> 00:05:57,648
Uh…

64
00:05:58,775 --> 00:06:00,818
Where's your mom?

65
00:06:00,902 --> 00:06:03,613
And why are you only with Papa?

66
00:06:04,530 --> 00:06:06,532
My mom is sick.

67
00:06:06,616 --> 00:06:10,578
She's… far away.

68
00:06:10,661 --> 00:06:13,372
Hmm… You're not taking care of her?

69
00:06:13,456 --> 00:06:14,832
[BEA] Um…

70
00:06:14,916 --> 00:06:17,752
Well, Oliver, uh…

71
00:06:17,835 --> 00:06:21,464
No one is allowed to go near her.

72
00:06:21,547 --> 00:06:26,928
But I know she's doing fine over there.

73
00:06:27,011 --> 00:06:31,140
And I'm fine, too, because…

74
00:06:32,308 --> 00:06:34,268
someone is taking care of me.

75
00:06:35,061 --> 00:06:36,312
Papa is.

76
00:06:38,272 --> 00:06:39,774
We brought some pastries.

77
00:06:39,857 --> 00:06:43,277
Billy and I bought this for you.

78
00:06:43,361 --> 00:06:44,862
- You bought it?
- Yes.

79
00:06:44,946 --> 00:06:46,280
With Billy?

80
00:06:46,364 --> 00:06:47,323
[CHUCKLES SOFTLY]

81
00:06:47,406 --> 00:06:48,324
Thank you.

82
00:06:49,325 --> 00:06:51,119
[BEA] Here, let's share it.

83
00:06:54,789 --> 00:06:56,207
As siblings do.

84
00:07:00,586 --> 00:07:02,547
[OLIVER] Just take whatever you want.

85
00:07:02,630 --> 00:07:03,965
- All right, I'll help myself.
- Yes.

86
00:07:04,632 --> 00:07:05,758
Mm.

87
00:07:05,842 --> 00:07:07,426
- Billy. Papa.
- This is a lot.

88
00:07:08,010 --> 00:07:09,595
Let's eat.

89
00:07:11,722 --> 00:07:13,516
Here. I'll get one for myself.

90
00:07:13,599 --> 00:07:14,851
- Okay.
- Thank you.

91
00:07:15,560 --> 00:07:16,936
[OLIVER] Papa. Billy.

92
00:07:17,603 --> 00:07:20,356
Here. Let's all eat.

93
00:07:21,691 --> 00:07:22,525
Oh, Oliver.

94
00:07:22,608 --> 00:07:25,570
Why did you bring sweets?

95
00:07:26,237 --> 00:07:27,822
[ENRICO] I'll eat just a bit.

96
00:07:27,905 --> 00:07:29,657
[BILLY] Dad, you can't eat those.

97
00:07:29,740 --> 00:07:30,783
You know that.

98
00:07:30,867 --> 00:07:33,035
- [OLIVER] Just a bit.
- I told you, he can't eat that.

99
00:07:33,119 --> 00:07:35,872
- [ENRICO] I'll take one bite.
- [OLIVER] Just one bite.

100
00:07:35,955 --> 00:07:42,211
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

101
00:07:48,050 --> 00:07:49,802
[BEA] <i>We'll get out of here, Ma.</i>

102
00:07:51,345 --> 00:07:53,264
<i>We'll rise up from this.</i>

103
00:07:54,140 --> 00:07:56,267
<i>And if you still love Papa,</i>

104
00:07:57,059 --> 00:07:59,645
<i>I'll take him back for you.</i>

105
00:08:00,271 --> 00:08:02,565
<i>Our family will be complete again.</i>

106
00:08:03,900 --> 00:08:10,907
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

107
00:08:17,788 --> 00:08:19,540
Here's your key.

108
00:08:20,416 --> 00:08:22,126
I'll visit you here often.

109
00:08:22,210 --> 00:08:23,628
I can come every day if you want.

110
00:08:23,711 --> 00:08:26,547
You know, I still can't believe

111
00:08:27,632 --> 00:08:29,133
that we're together again.

112
00:08:30,843 --> 00:08:31,802
Me neither.

113
00:08:31,886 --> 00:08:35,264
But it would be much better
if Mama were here too.

114
00:08:35,348 --> 00:08:37,725
You know we can't do that right now.

115
00:08:37,808 --> 00:08:39,644
Ah. By the way,

116
00:08:39,727 --> 00:08:42,438
these are from Billy.

117
00:08:42,980 --> 00:08:44,232
- All of this?
- Mm-hmm.

118
00:08:44,315 --> 00:08:46,025
- For me?
- Mm-hmm.

119
00:08:48,236 --> 00:08:49,195
Take a look.

120
00:08:50,404 --> 00:08:51,864
They're clothes.

121
00:08:51,948 --> 00:08:52,949
Here.

122
00:08:54,116 --> 00:08:56,827
- Billy gave me all these?
- Yes. And this too.

123
00:08:56,911 --> 00:08:59,038
So we can keep in touch with you.

124
00:08:59,121 --> 00:09:05,002
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

125
00:09:06,879 --> 00:09:07,964
Bea.

126
00:09:08,548 --> 00:09:09,465
Sorry about this.

127
00:09:09,549 --> 00:09:11,217
This was all I could do.

128
00:09:16,681 --> 00:09:17,682
Um…

129
00:09:19,642 --> 00:09:21,477
This is already too much.

130
00:09:22,436 --> 00:09:23,813
Thank you.

131
00:09:23,896 --> 00:09:26,899
[STAMMERS]
Please tell Billy I said thank you.

132
00:09:26,983 --> 00:09:32,321
It would have been enough that she
dropped the charges and forgave me.

133
00:09:32,405 --> 00:09:34,031
This is too much.

134
00:09:34,824 --> 00:09:39,120
P-please tell her that
I'm going to work hard.

135
00:09:39,203 --> 00:09:41,455
I'm going to find a job.

136
00:09:42,164 --> 00:09:45,751
And I promise that I'm going to change.

137
00:09:45,835 --> 00:09:48,212
Please tell Billy I'm going to change.

138
00:09:52,091 --> 00:09:53,509
I'm already very happy…

139
00:09:57,513 --> 00:09:58,806
that you're here now.

140
00:10:04,979 --> 00:10:06,147
<i>You know what?</i>

141
00:10:07,189 --> 00:10:12,236
<i>I can feel that your father</i>
<i>is genuinely sorry.</i>

142
00:10:13,571 --> 00:10:16,157
<i>Do you think</i>

143
00:10:17,116 --> 00:10:18,826
<i>he still loves me?</i>

144
00:10:20,036 --> 00:10:21,078
<i>Um…</i>

145
00:10:21,162 --> 00:10:25,499
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

146
00:10:25,583 --> 00:10:26,959
<i>That's possible, Ma.</i>

147
00:10:27,877 --> 00:10:29,712
<i>I was thinking the same thing.</i>

148
00:10:29,795 --> 00:10:30,838
<i>It's possible.</i>

149
00:10:31,881 --> 00:10:33,966
<i>But there's a problem.</i>

150
00:10:34,050 --> 00:10:37,637
<i>That Billy and her aunt.</i>

151
00:10:38,387 --> 00:10:39,930
<i>I hate sharing.</i>

152
00:10:40,014 --> 00:10:41,766
<i>No way.</i>

153
00:10:42,516 --> 00:10:44,143
<i>We are the first family.</i>

154
00:10:44,226 --> 00:10:45,478
<i>Billy.</i>

155
00:10:47,146 --> 00:10:48,439
<i>Billy, I'm begging you.</i>

156
00:10:48,522 --> 00:10:51,734
<i>If you drop the case against my mom,</i>

157
00:10:51,817 --> 00:10:54,403
<i>I promise I'll watch over her.</i>

158
00:10:54,487 --> 00:10:56,864
<i>I promise she won't bother you.</i>

159
00:10:56,947 --> 00:11:00,951
<i>I promise, Billy. Please.</i>
<i>Just withdraw the case against my mother.</i>

160
00:11:01,535 --> 00:11:02,620
<i>Please, Billy. Please.</i>

161
00:11:02,703 --> 00:11:04,747
<i>Have mercy on my mother. Please.</i>

162
00:11:05,414 --> 00:11:07,375
<i>If you were in my position,</i>

163
00:11:09,251 --> 00:11:13,422
<i>and your family had almost died</i>
<i>because of someone…</i>

164
00:11:16,258 --> 00:11:18,594
<i>would you really let her walk free?</i>

165
00:11:26,060 --> 00:11:27,478
Ms. Tere!

166
00:11:27,561 --> 00:11:28,396
Oh no.

167
00:11:28,479 --> 00:11:30,564
Ms. Tere, I've changed!

168
00:11:30,648 --> 00:11:32,691
I'll take on any job you give me.

169
00:11:32,775 --> 00:11:33,943
A job?

170
00:11:34,026 --> 00:11:35,528
You're an ex-convict.

171
00:11:35,611 --> 00:11:38,697
Who would trust you?

172
00:11:38,781 --> 00:11:40,157
No one.

173
00:11:40,241 --> 00:11:42,910
You might even make me lose customers.

174
00:11:42,993 --> 00:11:43,953
Oh, right!

175
00:11:44,036 --> 00:11:46,330
Why don't you ask your criminal boyfriend?

176
00:11:47,206 --> 00:11:49,417
- What did you say? Huh?
- [TERE SCREAMS]

177
00:11:49,500 --> 00:11:51,335
- Want me to show you--
- That's exactly my point!

178
00:11:51,419 --> 00:11:53,796
How can you get a job with that attitude?

179
00:11:53,879 --> 00:11:55,923
You're still evil as before!

180
00:11:56,006 --> 00:11:57,425
[GRUNTS] To hell with you!

181
00:11:59,218 --> 00:12:00,428
Damn you!

182
00:12:00,511 --> 00:12:05,850
[GRIM MUSIC PLAYING]

183
00:12:10,896 --> 00:12:13,899
<i>Do you know I'm getting</i>
<i>in trouble because of you?</i>

184
00:12:13,983 --> 00:12:15,401
<i>Because of what you've been doing.</i>

185
00:12:15,484 --> 00:12:17,361
<i>Because you refuse to leave me alone.</i>

186
00:12:17,445 --> 00:12:20,573
<i>So please, okay? Just leave me alone.</i>

187
00:12:20,656 --> 00:12:22,116
<i>Because they think</i>

188
00:12:22,199 --> 00:12:24,410
<i>we're accomplices.</i>

189
00:12:25,369 --> 00:12:27,288
<i>I could even go to jail because of you.</i>

190
00:12:27,371 --> 00:12:29,373
<i>So please, I'm begging you.</i>

191
00:12:29,457 --> 00:12:32,710
<i>Please, please. Stay away from me.</i>

192
00:12:37,465 --> 00:12:40,217
[LAUGHS]

193
00:12:40,301 --> 00:12:43,137
<i>Accomplices?! You got that right!</i>
<i>We're accomplices!</i>

194
00:12:43,220 --> 00:12:45,097
<i>Accomplices in love, right?</i>

195
00:12:45,681 --> 00:12:47,433
<i>That's how we do it.</i>

196
00:12:47,516 --> 00:12:49,435
<i>'Bi, you know I'm right.</i>

197
00:12:49,518 --> 00:12:51,270
<i>You love me. I know you do.</i>

198
00:12:51,353 --> 00:12:53,272
<i>'Bi, come on.</i>

199
00:12:53,355 --> 00:12:55,316
<i>That's how we do it…</i>

200
00:12:55,399 --> 00:12:57,401
<i>- Crazy! You're crazy!</i>
- [CALOY] <i>That's how, right?</i>

201
00:12:57,485 --> 00:12:58,986
<i>- No!</i>
- [BEA] <i>See, ma'am? He's crazy!</i>

202
00:12:59,069 --> 00:13:00,821
<i>What do you mean, "crazy?!"</i>
<i>I'm not crazy, 'Bi!</i>

203
00:13:00,905 --> 00:13:03,115
<i>- What I'm saying is true.</i>
- [BEA] <i>We only met once!</i>

204
00:13:03,199 --> 00:13:06,035
<i>It was just karaoke! Just one duet!</i>

205
00:13:06,118 --> 00:13:07,328
<i>And now you're harassing me?</i>

206
00:13:07,411 --> 00:13:09,205
<i>I'm going to get arrested because of you?!</i>

207
00:13:09,288 --> 00:13:10,581
<i>'Bi, what do you mean, harassing you?</i>

208
00:13:11,415 --> 00:13:13,501
<i>What I feel is real. You know that, 'Bi.</i>

209
00:13:13,584 --> 00:13:15,085
<i>You love me. I know you do!</i>

210
00:13:15,169 --> 00:13:16,921
<i>- I'm right, aren't I?</i>
- [BEA]<i> I don't--</i>

211
00:13:17,004 --> 00:13:18,297
<i>What do you mean, "love?!"</i>

212
00:13:18,380 --> 00:13:21,133
<i>How can I love you?! We only met once!</i>

213
00:13:21,217 --> 00:13:25,346
<i>Why do we even have to know each other</i>
<i>when it's true that we love each other?</i>

214
00:13:25,429 --> 00:13:27,348
<i>'Bi, I love you!</i>

215
00:13:27,431 --> 00:13:28,933
- [BEA]<i> Please.</i>
<i>- You know, when I get out--</i>

216
00:13:29,016 --> 00:13:30,935
<i>When I escape, we'll be together.</i>

217
00:13:31,018 --> 00:13:32,019
<i>We'll get rich, 'Bi.</i>

218
00:13:32,102 --> 00:13:34,104
<i>We'll become rich, 'Bi.</i>

219
00:13:34,188 --> 00:13:39,151
[GRIM MUSIC CONTINUES]

220
00:13:39,235 --> 00:13:41,570
The person you're looking for isn't here.

221
00:13:41,654 --> 00:13:45,699
Carlos Toledo was one of the prisoners
who escaped last week.

222
00:13:46,575 --> 00:13:47,618
Escaped?

223
00:13:47,701 --> 00:13:51,330
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

224
00:13:51,413 --> 00:13:53,165
I'm here to visit Mr. Santos.

225
00:13:53,249 --> 00:13:54,500
Mm.

226
00:14:01,924 --> 00:14:03,467
[MUSIC FADES]

227
00:14:05,511 --> 00:14:06,512
[BEA] Wilfred.

228
00:14:07,555 --> 00:14:08,472
[WILFRED] Hey.

229
00:14:08,556 --> 00:14:10,266
Look at you.

230
00:14:10,349 --> 00:14:11,892
They let you out already?

231
00:14:12,518 --> 00:14:14,520
Don't tell me you followed
in Caloy's footsteps.

232
00:14:14,603 --> 00:14:15,604
You ran away too, didn't you?

233
00:14:16,230 --> 00:14:19,567
If you're here to ask for help
with a fake passport, I'm gonna pass.

234
00:14:19,650 --> 00:14:22,528
- I'm done dealing with fugitives.
- [BEA] You talk way too much.

235
00:14:22,611 --> 00:14:24,822
I just want to know where Caloy is.

236
00:14:25,531 --> 00:14:26,490
Do you know?

237
00:14:26,574 --> 00:14:28,242
You know where he is, don't you, Wilfred?

238
00:14:29,159 --> 00:14:30,953
Just leave me alone, all right?

239
00:14:31,996 --> 00:14:33,080
- Leave you alone?
- Ouch!

240
00:14:33,163 --> 00:14:34,707
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

241
00:14:34,790 --> 00:14:37,084
Want me to call the cops on you, huh?

242
00:14:37,167 --> 00:14:38,294
[WILFRED] Hey, give those back!

243
00:14:38,377 --> 00:14:40,462
- Those belong to my customer!
- Where's Caloy?

244
00:14:41,964 --> 00:14:43,382
Where's Caloy?!

245
00:14:51,140 --> 00:14:56,228
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

246
00:15:02,026 --> 00:15:03,068
[CAR BEEPING]

247
00:15:20,169 --> 00:15:21,378
[ENGINE STARTS]

248
00:15:21,462 --> 00:15:24,924
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

249
00:15:25,007 --> 00:15:26,675
[GEARSHIFT CLICKING]

250
00:15:32,348 --> 00:15:33,474
[TIRES SCREECH]

251
00:15:39,939 --> 00:15:43,984
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

252
00:15:44,068 --> 00:15:45,152
[CAR DOOR OPENS]

253
00:15:46,820 --> 00:15:47,905
[CAR DOOR CLOSES]

254
00:15:55,162 --> 00:15:59,375
[THRILLING MUSIC PLAYING]

255
00:15:59,458 --> 00:16:00,501
[GRUNTS SOFTLY]

256
00:16:13,973 --> 00:16:20,980
[THRILLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

257
00:16:23,273 --> 00:16:28,404
[PHONE RINGING]

258
00:16:40,708 --> 00:16:41,583
Caloy?

259
00:16:42,292 --> 00:16:43,168
Bea?

260
00:16:43,252 --> 00:16:44,503
Caloy, where are you?

261
00:16:44,586 --> 00:16:45,671
Let's meet.

262
00:16:45,754 --> 00:16:51,885
[THRILLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

263
00:16:51,969 --> 00:16:54,013
[MUSIC FADING]

264
00:16:55,222 --> 00:16:58,267
[UNSETTLING MUSIC PLAYING]

265
00:16:58,350 --> 00:17:05,232
[FOOTSTEPS APPROACHING]

266
00:17:11,196 --> 00:17:12,239
[BEA] Caloy?

267
00:17:12,906 --> 00:17:14,158
[UNSETTLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

268
00:17:14,241 --> 00:17:15,534
Bea.

269
00:17:16,618 --> 00:17:17,453
Caloy.

270
00:17:18,454 --> 00:17:20,539
[BOTH LAUGHING SOFTLY]

271
00:17:20,622 --> 00:17:21,957
[CALOY] I missed you.

272
00:17:24,918 --> 00:17:26,128
I love you.

273
00:17:27,212 --> 00:17:29,006
- I missed you.
- [CHUCKLES SOFTLY]

274
00:17:29,506 --> 00:17:31,508
W-What happened to you?

275
00:17:31,592 --> 00:17:34,011
I looked for you. I-It was-- Goodness.

276
00:17:34,094 --> 00:17:35,554
How did you get out?

277
00:17:36,305 --> 00:17:37,264
Uh…

278
00:17:37,347 --> 00:17:38,682
[UNSETTLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

279
00:17:38,766 --> 00:17:39,892
Because of Billy.

280
00:17:40,476 --> 00:17:41,977
Billy forgave me.

281
00:17:44,438 --> 00:17:45,647
Really?

282
00:17:46,607 --> 00:17:47,649
How?

283
00:17:48,442 --> 00:17:49,610
And why?

284
00:17:52,362 --> 00:17:53,322
Caloy…

285
00:17:53,405 --> 00:17:57,493
[UNSETTLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

286
00:17:57,576 --> 00:17:59,244
Billy and I are half-sisters.

287
00:18:01,413 --> 00:18:07,503
[MUSIC BECOMES DRAMATIC]

288
00:18:09,254 --> 00:18:13,175
<i>I won't let that half-sister of yours</i>
<i>bully you anymore.</i>

289
00:18:13,759 --> 00:18:15,135
<i>I'll take both her and Jordan down.</i>

290
00:18:15,719 --> 00:18:16,720
<i>Hey.</i>

291
00:18:17,221 --> 00:18:18,722
<i>- No.</i>
<i>- Calm down.</i>

292
00:18:18,806 --> 00:18:19,848
<i>No.</i>

293
00:18:19,932 --> 00:18:21,183
<i>Stop it, Caloy.</i>

294
00:18:21,266 --> 00:18:22,684
<i>They're on high alert because of you.</i>

295
00:18:22,768 --> 00:18:25,979
<i>If something bad happens</i>
<i>to Billy and her family,</i>

296
00:18:26,063 --> 00:18:28,398
<i>I'm sure the blame will fall on me.</i>

297
00:18:30,692 --> 00:18:34,196
<i>I can tell that Billy is still mad at me,</i>

298
00:18:34,780 --> 00:18:36,073
<i>but guess what?</i>

299
00:18:36,156 --> 00:18:38,283
<i>She gave me a cell phone,</i>

300
00:18:40,077 --> 00:18:43,622
<i>clothes, and even cash.</i>

301
00:18:44,164 --> 00:18:46,125
<i>What happened?</i>

302
00:18:48,085 --> 00:18:51,004
<i>After everything we worked for,</i>
<i>you gave in to bribes.</i>

303
00:18:51,088 --> 00:18:53,507
<i>There's so much going on</i>
<i>in your life right now,</i>

304
00:18:53,590 --> 00:18:56,009
<i>and yet you're still hanging in there.</i>

305
00:18:58,303 --> 00:19:02,558
<i>Promise. From now on,</i>
<i>we will do better.</i>

306
00:19:03,934 --> 00:19:05,018
<i>No.</i>

307
00:19:07,146 --> 00:19:09,982
<i>I'm the one who needs to</i>
<i>apologize to you all.</i>

308
00:19:12,151 --> 00:19:13,402
<i>I'm sorry.</i>

309
00:19:14,278 --> 00:19:16,947
<i>Sometimes, I end up taking</i>
<i>my anger out on you.</i>

310
00:19:17,823 --> 00:19:20,534
<i>It's okay, we understand.</i>

311
00:19:22,286 --> 00:19:23,996
<i>So, how are things</i>
<i>between you and your sister?</i>

312
00:19:27,124 --> 00:19:28,750
<i>I wouldn't call her that.</i>

313
00:19:30,002 --> 00:19:31,253
<i>Ahh!</i>

314
00:19:31,336 --> 00:19:32,337
<i>Hey!</i>

315
00:19:33,088 --> 00:19:36,175
<i>- You can scream here.</i>
<i>- No, you can't!</i>

316
00:19:36,258 --> 00:19:37,843
[BOTH CHUCKLE SOFTLY]

317
00:19:37,926 --> 00:19:41,680
<i>If my gigs can't take</i>
<i>your stress away,</i>

318
00:19:42,556 --> 00:19:43,891
<i>then this might help.</i>

319
00:19:43,974 --> 00:19:45,517
<i>- Come on, give it a try.</i>
<i>- I don't think so.</i>

320
00:19:45,601 --> 00:19:46,643
<i>Let's do it together.</i>

321
00:19:47,769 --> 00:19:48,979
<i>No!</i>

322
00:19:49,062 --> 00:19:50,147
<i>Don't do it!</i>

323
00:19:50,230 --> 00:19:52,357
[BOTH CHUCKLING SOFTLY]

324
00:19:52,441 --> 00:19:53,442
<i>There.</i>

325
00:19:54,610 --> 00:19:55,986
<i>I'm just happy that…</i>

326
00:19:57,863 --> 00:20:00,324
<i>I made you feel a bit lighter.</i>

327
00:20:00,407 --> 00:20:03,952
<i>I'm sorry that I haven't been able</i>
<i>to catch your gigs lately.</i>

328
00:20:04,036 --> 00:20:05,996
<i>I'm sorry, too,</i>

329
00:20:06,079 --> 00:20:08,999
<i>that we don't get to celebrate your wins.</i>

330
00:20:09,666 --> 00:20:10,959
<i>I'm such a terrible best friend.</i>

331
00:20:11,043 --> 00:20:12,961
<i>You've always been there for me,</i>

332
00:20:13,045 --> 00:20:14,713
<i>but I let you down.</i>

333
00:20:14,796 --> 00:20:17,883
<i>Even if you don't say a word, I get you.</i>

334
00:20:21,011 --> 00:20:22,888
<i>But still, thank you for the apology</i>

335
00:20:22,971 --> 00:20:24,056
<i>because…</i>

336
00:20:25,807 --> 00:20:27,559
<i>you've been kind of rude lately, you know?</i>

337
00:20:30,187 --> 00:20:32,064
<i>Ma! What are you doing?</i>

338
00:20:32,147 --> 00:20:34,650
[MARIELA SOBS]

339
00:20:34,733 --> 00:20:35,901
<i>Sorry about that.</i>

340
00:20:38,779 --> 00:20:41,114
<i>- Ma…</i>
<i>- Why did you only visit me now?</i>

341
00:20:41,198 --> 00:20:42,658
<i>Look!</i>

342
00:20:42,741 --> 00:20:45,869
<i>This is what they're doing to me!</i>
<i>They're hurting me!</i>

343
00:20:45,953 --> 00:20:47,621
<i>Ma'am, that's not true.</i>

344
00:20:47,704 --> 00:20:49,581
<i>She was extremely distressed</i>
<i>the other night.</i>

345
00:20:49,665 --> 00:20:52,709
<i>She wouldn't calm down</i>
<i>and ended up hurting herself.</i>

346
00:20:52,793 --> 00:20:54,211
<i>- This is your fault!</i>
<i>- Ma.</i>

347
00:20:54,836 --> 00:20:55,963
<i>Enough.</i>

348
00:20:56,046 --> 00:20:57,256
<i>Shh.</i>

349
00:20:58,006 --> 00:21:01,051
<i>Didn't I tell you to behave here?</i>

350
00:21:01,635 --> 00:21:03,345
<i>Endure it a little longer.</i>

351
00:21:03,428 --> 00:21:05,681
<i>I'll get you out of here soon, okay?</i>

352
00:21:05,764 --> 00:21:07,057
<i>When exactly?</i>
